      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #83): A!B for a small non-negative integer A
      ⍝ (K) used to always compute Γ(1+B)÷(Γ(1+A)×Γ(1+B-A)), which
      ⍝ overflows once B alone is large enough that Γ(1+B) is infinite
      ⍝ (roughly B ≥ 170), even though the true quotient (B choose K) is
      ⍝ a perfectly ordinary finite number for huge B and small K.
      ⍝ real_binomial() now computes the equivalent product formula
      ⍝ ∏(B-i)÷K! directly for such A, which stays finite.
      ⍝
