      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs31 #15): bif_binomial()'s int64
      ⍝ fast path took A/B as "integer" whenever is_near_int64_t() held,
      ⍝ using the fixed absolute INTEGER_TOLERANCE (1E¯10) -- so a
      ⍝ genuinely nonzero-but-tiny N (e.g. 1E¯11, 1E¯100) snapped to the
      ⍝ exact integer 0, after which the row's '0' case returned 0
      ⍝ outright instead of reaching the true (nonzero) Gamma-based
      ⍝ answer. Tolerant snap-to-integer belongs to =/≠'s ⎕CT, not to !.
      ⍝
